From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:41:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: three-column labeled Quick Settings grid, four-tile
 compact row

The Titan 2 Quick Settings artifact shows the expanded controls as three
columns of small square tiles, each named under its icon, and the compact
shade as one row of four small tiles. Upstream compose QS uses one
column count for both and draws small tiles icon-only, which is why the
Q25 used two large columns before.

* config_sableQuickQsNumColumns (default 0 = the grid's count) gives the
  compact row its own column count, read by
  QuickQuickSettingsRowRepository and used by QuickQuickSettingsViewModel
  unless media shares the row.
* config_sableQsSmallTileLabels (default false) makes a small tile show
  its label under a 24dp icon (SableLabeledSmallTileContent). The label
  is decoration; the tile's semantics already carry name and state.

Defaults keep upstream behaviour; SableSystemUIOverlay sets 4 and true
and the grid column count to 3. Keys from 0303 (Space, Alt+Enter) are
unchanged.
